<reference id="_Toc235450432" xml:lang="en-us">
   <title>Scenario 4 — Equation in a list item</title>
   <shortdesc>Consider a &lt;ul&gt; list where one of the &lt;li&gt; items contains a &lt;math&gt; element inline</shortdesc>
  <prolog>
    <metadata>
      <keywords>
        <keyword>inline</keyword>
        <keyword>Equation</keyword>
        <keyword>element</keyword>
        <keyword>within</keyword>
        <keyword>Scenario</keyword>
        <keyword>DITA</keyword>
        <indexterm>inline</indexterm>
        <indexterm>Equation</indexterm>
        <indexterm>element</indexterm>
      </keywords>
      <prodinfo>
        <prodname></prodname>
      </prodinfo>
    </metadata>
  </prolog>
   <refbody>
      <section>
      <p>Consider a <codeph>&lt;ul&gt;</codeph> list where one of the <codeph>&lt;li&gt;</codeph> items contains a <codeph>&lt;math&gt;</codeph> element inline within the item text.</p>
         <table frame="all" colsep="1" rowsep="1">
            <title>Equation in a list item</title>
            <tgroup cols="2">
               <colspec colname="c1"/>
               <colspec colname="c2"/>
               <thead>
                  <row>
                     <entry>
                        <b>HTML Input</b>
                     </entry>
                     <entry>
                        <b>DITA Output</b>
                     </entry>
                  </row>
               </thead>
               <tbody>
                  <row>
                     <entry>
                        <codeblock>
&lt;ul>
  &lt;li>
    Use the formula
    &lt;math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML">
      &lt;mrow>
        &lt;mi>A&lt;/mi>
        &lt;mo>=&lt;/mo>
        &lt;mi>π&lt;/mi>
        &lt;msup>
          &lt;mi>r&lt;/mi>
          &lt;mn>2&lt;/mn>
        &lt;/msup>
      &lt;/mrow>
    &lt;/math>
    to calculate area.
  &lt;/li>
  &lt;li>
    Round results to two decimal places.
  &lt;/li>
&lt;/ul></codeblock>
                     </entry>
                     <entry>
                        <codeblock>
&lt;ul>
  &lt;li>
    Use the formula
    &lt;equation-inline>
      &lt;mathml>
        &lt;math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML">
          &lt;mrow>
            &lt;mi>A&lt;/mi>
            &lt;mo>=&lt;/mo>
            &lt;mi>π&lt;/mi>
            &lt;msup>
              &lt;mi>r&lt;/mi>
              &lt;mn>2&lt;/mn>
            &lt;/msup>
          &lt;/mrow>
        &lt;/math>
      &lt;/mathml>
    &lt;/equation-inline>
    to calculate area.
  &lt;/li>
  &lt;li>
    Round results to two decimal places.
  &lt;/li>
&lt;/ul></codeblock>
                     </entry>
                  </row>
               </tbody>
            </tgroup>
         </table>
<p><b>Result:</b> When a <codeph>&lt;math&gt;</codeph> element is embedded inline within a <codeph>&lt;li&gt;</codeph> item, the converter preserves it as an <codeph>&lt;equation-inline&gt;</codeph> element inside the DITA <codeph>&lt;li&gt;</codeph>. The equation is treated as part of the list item's inline content and remains within the list structure.</p>
   </section>
   </refbody>
</reference>
